      {
       "id": "51060b30",
       "settings": {
        "html": "<div class=\"faq-list\"><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-1\" id=\"faq-1-t\">What cities and areas in Central Iowa do you service for heating repair? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-1-t\"><p><b>Lenz Heating &amp; Cooling provides 24/7 heating, furnace, and heater services across the Greater Des Moines metro area.</b> Our primary service locations include Des Moines, Urbandale, Waukee, West Des Moines, Ankeny, Johnston, Clive, Grimes, Norwalk, and surrounding Polk and Dallas County communities. Call <b>(515) 225-6446</b> to schedule fast heating service in your neighborhood.</p></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-2\" id=\"faq-2-t\">Why is my furnace or heater blowing cold air? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-2-t\"><p><b>A furnace blowing cold air is typically caused by a dirty air filter restricting airflow, a tripped limit switch, an extinguished pilot light, or a faulty flame sensor.</b> Check that your thermostat is set to \"AUTO\" rather than \"ON\" so the fan doesn't run continuously when heat isn't actively generating.</p></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-3\" id=\"faq-3-t\">How much does furnace or heating repair cost in Des Moines? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-3-t\"><p><b>Heating repair in Des Moines typically costs between $150 and $600 for common issues like igniter, flame sensor, or pressure switch replacements.</b> Complex motor or heat exchanger repairs can cost $800 or more. Lenz Heating &amp; Cooling provides flat-rate diagnostic pricing before work begins.</p></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-4\" id=\"faq-4-t\">What should I do if my heating stops working in the middle of the night? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-4-t\"><p><b>If your heating stops working in the middle of the night, follow these steps before calling for emergency repair:</b></p><ul><li>Verify your thermostat switch is set to \"HEAT\" with working batteries.</li><li>Ensure your furnace power switch and electrical circuit breaker are turned on.</li><li>Check for a completely clogged air filter restricting airflow.</li><li>If heat doesn't return, call <b>Lenz Heating &amp; Cooling at (515) 225-6446</b> for 24/7 dispatch.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-5\" id=\"faq-5-t\">How long does a gas furnace or home heater usually last in Iowa? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-5-t\"><p><b>A gas furnace or home heater typically lasts 15 to 20 years in Central Iowa.</b> Severe Midwest winter weather places heavy demands on heating systems. Annual furnace tune-ups, regular filter changes every 1 to 3 months, and clean ductwork are required to reach the 20-year lifespan.</p></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-6\" id=\"faq-6-t\">Should I repair or replace my aging furnace or heater? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-6\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-6-t\"><p><b>You should replace your furnace if the system is over 15 years old and repair costs equal 50% or more of a new unit's price.</b> Additionally, if winter heating bills are steadily climbing despite regular maintenance, installing a high-efficiency 96%+ AFUE furnace provides long-term energy savings.</p></div></div><div class=\"faq\"><h3 style=\"margin:0\"><button class=\"faq__trigger\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"faq-7\" id=\"faq-7-t\">How often should I schedule furnace maintenance or a heater tune-up? <svg class=\"faq__icon icon-sm\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg></button></h3><div class=\"faq__panel\" id=\"faq-7\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-7-t\"><p><b>You should schedule furnace maintenance once per year, ideally in early autumn before cold weather begins.</b> Annual tune-ups clean burners, inspect heat exchangers for dangerous carbon monoxide leaks, optimize fuel efficiency, and prevent emergency winter breakdowns.</p></div></div></div>"
       },
